# Day 08 – ADAS (Advanced Driver Assistance System)

## Objective
Implemented the ADAS layer for the EV Dashboard project using ultrasonic sensor data and vehicle speed.

## Features Implemented

- Forward Collision Warning (FCW)
- Time to Collision (TTC) calculation
- Critical collision detection
- Blind Spot Detection (BSD)
- Overspeed detection
- Alarm priority management
- Hysteresis to prevent alarm flickering
- Collision and blind-spot LED indication

## Thresholds

| Feature | Threshold |
|---|---|
| FCW Warning | < 50 cm |
| FCW Critical | < 20 cm |
| TTC Warning | < 3 seconds |
| TTC Critical | < 1.5 seconds |
| Blind Spot | < 30 cm |
| BSD Speed Gate | > 20 km/h |
| Overspeed | > 120 km/h |

## Files

- `adas.c` – ADAS logic and alarm processing
- `adas.h` – ADAS structures, thresholds and APIs

## Input

ADAS receives:
- Front ultrasonic distance
- Left ultrasonic distance
- Right ultrasonic distance
- Vehicle speed

## Output

- Collision warning level
- Blind spot status
- Overspeed status
- Overall alarm priority
- Warning LEDs
